Plus, the inevitable opposition that flares up? Immediately tagged as being in league with Aberrant by the media. Not hurt by the fact that in some cases it will be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If one is going for Totalitarian control, it's an effective cudgel. And if true, well so much the better because people doing the research will find you are not lying. And given that Abberants are by in large twisted mockeries of Humanity at that point, justified Xenophobia will go a long way to helping establish control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","user":"TheWanderingJewels","date":". 02-14-2019, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:46:40-08:00","id":1287955,"title":"","content":"Yeah I always wondered when they would crack down on potential telepathic manipulations, especially if the Doyen are discovered.<br /> <br /> And corporations, especially Megacorporations aren\u2019t confined to one Country, so a collection of Megacorps take over North America but what the rest of the world don\u2019t boycott them? It makes more sense in a setting where everyone is dystopian, but Aeon is a mishmash of all the Genres so I\u2019m not sure how they handle this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:53:11-08:00","id":1288018,"title":"","content":"Honestly the FSA got hit hard not just because of all the American Novas but.. all the immigrant Novas. Brain/Nova drain is probably an issue for many countries where they flock to america to make easy money there's probably the highest percentage of Novas to norms so.. the fact that the FSA isn't full on Mad max wasteland is fairly optimstic given the timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:34:52-08:00","id":1288038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288018#post1288018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the FSA got hit hard not just because of all the American Novas but.. all the immigrant Novas. Brain/Nova drain is probably an issue for many countries where they flock to america to make easy money there's probably the highest percentage of Novas to norms so.. the fact that the FSA isn't full on Mad max wasteland is fairly optimstic given the timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, USA had lots of novas that where there for money, not fighting wars like in Africa, but living there. They probably had the largest nova population in the world, a few places could have a larger nova/baseline balance, but as USA had a large population, large area and lots of money to pay.<br /> <br /> China is more closed than any other country (except North Korea), so I guess many Chinese novas left and not many foreigners got in.<br /> India and Indonesia have huge populations but are fairly poor and would not attract novas as USA and would repel many of their own novas for religious if not just for the money.<br /> Next country in population is USA, so probably the largest nova population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-14-2019, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:50:00-08:00","id":1288043,"title":"","content":"Still, America as Fascist wasteland is a worn out cliche. It has been decades since a positive and democratic vision of America's future has been part of popular culture. Rehashing this cliche seems right-wing as if the FSA and societies like it were less warnings and more wishes. America as hell hole has been done to death and each new iteration of the trope sounds more like praise of Fascism not a warning against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:06:26-08:00","id":1288068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288043#post1288043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, America as Fascist wasteland is a worn out cliche. It has been decades since a positive and democratic vision of America's future has been part of popular culture. Rehashing this cliche seems right-wing as if the FSA and societies like it were less warnings and more wishes. America as hell hole has been done to death and each new iteration of the trope sounds more like praise of Fascism not a warning against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been years since a positive and democratic vision of Humanity\u2019s future has been part of popular culture. I think since Strar Treck there is no one popular item that is really positive, even the last Star Treck s\u00e9ries and movies are quite negative compared to TOS.<br /> <br /> The view of the population from the government has changed the last decade and all the popularisation of the conspiration theories helps a lot this effect. There is also a right wing tendency on the world for a few years, after a quite long left wing position mainly in Europe and South America, that brings this fear of a neo-facist rising on first world countries. Fear leads to anger. Anger leads to hate. Hate leads to suffering. Hate leads to dystopian futures on the fiction... that\u2019s the dark side...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:24:28-08:00","id":1288077,"title":"","content":"Never be confused by the terms Left or Right. It's more of those who wish to be left to their own devices vs those who have this overweening need to be in every ones else's business for (fill in blank) reasons. Religion, Ideology, etc. Take your pick. The FSA does have nuance built into the area. One simply has to learn to look where.<br /> <br /> Which is why up thread I noticed someone considered the fact of various resistance movements of various types as a possible background option for adventures. They will be there and in spite of what FSA propaganda might be pushing, there are going to be a lot of people outside FSA 'protection' for various reasons. and so they will be 'off the grid' in some respects. how successful they will be depends on the level of resources they have access to and how out of the way from FSA attention they can be. The FSA is damned big. They cannot be everywhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T00:01:16-08:00","id":1288194,"title":"","content":"\u2018Positive and democratic America\u2019 isn\u2019t a popular sci-fi trope because it\u2019s boring and, quite honestly, feels like pandering to Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T02:37:38-08:00","id":1288216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288194#post1288194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2018Positive and democratic America\u2019 isn\u2019t a popular sci-fi trope because it\u2019s boring and, quite honestly, feels like pandering to Americans.</div> </div> </div> </div>? Then is positive insert country always pandering? And how isn\u2019t Grimmdark dystopian America cliche and masturbatory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:20:29-08:00","id":1288237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288216#post1288216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ? Then is positive insert country always pandering? And how isn\u2019t Grimmdark dystopian America cliche and masturbatory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Positive insert country isn\u2019t always pandering because the writers aren\u2019t always trying to sell to a given market. And dystopian USA is a cliche because it is popular, and it\u2019s popular because it is interesting. \u2018USA: everything is just fine!\u2019 is boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:32:45-08:00","id":1288293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288038#post1288038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, USA had lots of novas that where there for money, not fighting wars like in Africa, but living there. They probably had the largest nova population in the world, a few places could have a larger nova/baseline balance, but as USA had a large population, large area and lots of money to pay.<br /> <br /> China is more closed than any other country (except North Korea), so I guess many Chinese novas left and not many foreigners got in.<br /> India and Indonesia have huge populations but are fairly poor and would not attract novas as USA and would repel many of their own novas for religious if not just for the money.<br /> Next country in population is USA, so probably the largest nova population.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> China isn't North Korea now, or even in the Nova Age. Its just ALOT of Chinese Novas would probably leave because they can make more money elsewhere and China can't keep a teleporter in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:34:49-08:00","id":1288295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288043#post1288043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, America as Fascist wasteland is a worn out cliche. It has been decades since a positive and democratic vision of America's future has been part of popular culture. Rehashing this cliche seems right-wing as if the FSA and societies like it were less warnings and more wishes. America as hell hole has been done to death and each new iteration of the trope sounds more like praise of Fascism not a warning against it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly don't see how you can get through an apocalypse where the USA doesn't take the Brunt of it. Which is going to effect things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:56:24-08:00","id":1288304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288293#post1288293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> China isn't North Korea now, or even in the Nova Age. Its just ALOT of Chinese Novas would probably leave because they can make more money elsewhere and China can't keep a teleporter in.</div> </div> </div> </div>China is not North Korea, it\u2019s not sealed, it\u2019s not impossible to visit or to move there, but it\u2019s closed enough to be hard to move in. It\u2019s hard to find foreigners there, at least much more difficult than finding Chinese people elsewhere. Their culture is quite different and hard to adapt if you are used to the western ways. Chinese companies would pay novas a lot of money to work there, but the comfort for a Nova living on US would be greater than living on China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:46:46-08:00","id":1288345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288304#post1288304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> China is not North Korea, it\u2019s not sealed, it\u2019s not impossible to visit or to move there, but it\u2019s closed enough to be hard to move in. It\u2019s hard to find foreigners there, at least much more difficult than finding Chinese people elsewhere. Their culture is quite different and hard to adapt if you are used to the western ways. Chinese companies would pay novas a lot of money to work there, but the comfort for a Nova living on US would be greater than living on China.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s actuallyrathwr easy to move there if you have business concerns or want to teach English, I have a ton of friends and associates who did just that. In the Nova Age though they will probably Tighten their borders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:07:21-08:00","id":1288456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288295#post1288295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I honestly don't see how you can get through an apocalypse where the USA doesn't take the Brunt of it. Which is going to effect things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can put the USA through Hell in many different ways. Why simply offer a worn out cliche?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:13:48-08:00","id":1288485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288304#post1288304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> China is not North Korea, it\u2019s not sealed, it\u2019s not impossible to visit or to move there, but it\u2019s closed enough to be hard to move in. It\u2019s hard to find foreigners there, at least much more difficult than finding Chinese people elsewhere. Their culture is quite different and hard to adapt if you are used to the western ways. Chinese companies would pay novas a lot of money to work there, but the comfort for a Nova living on US would be greater than living on China.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right I mean, even Most Chinese Novas would probably find the US offers a greater level of comfort. Which is why the USA gets hit harder than other nations because it takes in more novas on average.. and more likely the ones who have less connection to people(so the ones who are more likely to go crazy!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288456#post1288456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can put the USA through Hell in many different ways. Why simply offer a worn out cliche?</div> </div> </div> </div>So would a complete colapse into Mad max have been less cliched? I don't see how you get from Nova age to Apocalypse without the USA taking the brunt of it. I mean we could have a bunch of USA successor states taking up North America But that would lead to its own cliches. We could have the Republic of Gilead.. oh wait too cliched... we could have the USA completely uninhabitable! like the survivors are refugees in Mexico and China.. I can totally not see how that would be painfully on the nose...<br /> <br /> I mean honestly given that the setting requires the USA to be hit hard and that its not coming out of it a super power. How would you run it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:19:48-08:00","id":1288488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288345#post1288345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s actuallyrathwr easy to move there if you have business concerns or want to teach English, I have a ton of friends and associates who did just that. In the Nova Age though they will probably Tighten their borders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is and it isn't. The whole situation with visas is currently complex. But while you can LIVE in China the rules still apply differently to you than citizens. Conversely at first I Imagine there are laws that make it SUPER EASY to naturalize as a Nova in the USA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T20:43:16-08:00","id":1288507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288488#post1288488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is and it isn't. The whole situation with visas is currently complex. But while you can LIVE in China the rules still apply differently to you than citizens. Conversely at first I Imagine there are laws that make it SUPER EASY to naturalize as a Nova in the USA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say anything about becoming a citizen I said live their, legal like. They are more concerned over the last few years but it\u2019s super easy to get a job teaching there if English is your native language and you aren\u2019t some sort of spy or security risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T10:38:22-08:00","id":1288638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288485#post1288485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean honestly given that the setting requires the USA to be hit hard and that it is not coming out of it a superpower. How would you run it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given the resources and size of the USA, we are likely to be a power unless prevented from healing. I know that dismissing the American people as worthless filth has become a trope. But the kind of crisis outlined has tended to bring positive growth in America's past, why assume a one-note corporate fascist state is the only future for America? Moreover, given that this world is heavily weighted toward China, why are we assuming that China, which is still proudly imperialist and ethnocentric doesn't demand the kind of power/control the USA is routinely accused of having now?<br /> <br /> It seems like it is taken as fact that the USA is the sole source of the world's evil and corruption. This is both silly and borders on several kinds of bigotry that deny adult agency to most human beings.<br /> <br /> As to the question, why not simply have a poorly recovered USA with competing visions of the good and the future. Corporations could, as in most of today's world, simply have too much power and thus imperial democracy. But there could be strong political movements fighting back. A divided decentralized USA prevents the people of the USA from having the power to fully reassert their rights. Corporations allied with religious and cultural conservatives could be fighting to maintain the fragmentation because it leaves them in the driver's seat. Outside groups like the Chinese, Norsa, or Proteus, all of whom dislike the idea of a revived America could aid the Corporate elites. This could give you a weakened America with cyberpunk stylings but it wouldn't be a bog standard &quot;EVIL AMERIKKKA!!&quot; In fact, the politics would be far livelier and there would be more chances for adventure and drama because the society would be in flux. Small scale victories could be achieved that changed lives for the better without being immediately followed by a Civil War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T12:06:24-08:00","id":1288667,"title":"","content":"Yeah it\u2019s pandery. The Authors are mostly American so they think they can get away with criticism of the homeland, as well as high five points. But they don\u2019t want the clap back of saying say China collapsed in on itself. <br /> <br /> Hell I surprised they had the gual to mention the Dalai Lama is in exile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:07:15-08:00","id":1288729,"title":"","content":"I can definitely see a Fall of the United States scenario, and the rise of a totalitarian state in its wake. What doesn't ring true to me about TC:\u00c6on's FSA is the choice of villain. I can even buy a military takeover backed by corporate interests and supported by a form of Christianity. But in all three cases, there's a subtext that these are natural developments for these groups given the circumstances, rather than aberrations. <br /> <br /> I don't buy the notion that social or religious conservatives would like or stand for these developments, let alone being the driving force behind them. Which is why my approach is to introduce specific personalities that have subverted the groups in question (e.g., my reference to Reverend Nehemiah Scudder) as well as prominent inclusion of the non-subverted parts of these groups in the resistance against the FSA. (It's also why I can't take seriously shows like the Handmaiden's Tale or Revolution; they strike me as dealing with caricatures of conservatives rather than anything resembling the real thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:54:42-08:00","id":1288746,"title":"","content":"To me it seems the the current writers just kept the first edition broad setting outline almost entirely as it was. Honestly, I can't complain about that, especially as I kept on asking to make sure that they kept certain figures still there (like Divis Mal) and also how I complained about how mummy the curse entirely too away everything that came before in the mummy line. (Related as this is the same company.)<br /> <br /> That said I also have to agree with the people who say the official version is not really an interesting way to go about doing it. In fact I'll be honest and say I didn't really like it in the old version. But back then it was actually kind of unique since we didn't look towards the future with such sadness.<br /> <br /> So personally I would prefer the post Aberrant War era to have a quite a lt of difficulties but that in the present time it's been healing and repairing itself and so it is still considered the United States of America rather than the FSA.<br /> <br /> All I know is that I'm glad that I'm one of those who look at the Aberrant book and don't automatically assume that it has to lead into the Aeon book. That from an internal perspective the timeline is still open ended. (Actually the whole multiverse thing of the second edition Trinity is really one of the best things that they could have done. That way nobody's forced automatically make an earlier game have to end in darkness and despair because of a later games starting point.)<br /> <br /> We know officially that they're not going to change it. It's the FSA and the America is basically a pit of dispair. And nothing says we have to keep it that way and I loan versions of the game. So I say why don't we come up with ideas on how either the darkness of the war could lead to something good or the FSA we could be only temporary for something better. If we can come up with some sort of nifty alternate timeline we could create a variant way to play the game. Heck I could see somebody from the official history finding a way to the alternate history to try to see how to make a better universe or vice a versa. Or even someone like Max Mercer who travels through Dimensions can see the good version and then go back to his original version and try to fix things.<br /> <br /> We have options as soon as we don't automatically feel that we need to stick to canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T15:48:44-08:00","id":1288761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288746#post1288746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it seems the the current writers just kept the first edition broad setting outline almost entirely as it was. Honestly, I can't complain about that, especially as I kept on asking to make sure that they kept certain figures still there (like Divis Mal) and also how I complained about how mummy the curse entirely too away everything that came before in the mummy line. (Related as this is the same company.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Mummy: the Curse isn't a second edition, so I don't see the rationale behind that one; but I'm with you in the rest. Still, that's a subject for a different forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288746#post1288746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that I'm glad that I'm one of those who look at the Aberrant book and don't automatically assume that it has to lead into the Aeon book. That from an internal perspective the timeline is still open ended. (Actually the whole multiverse thing of the second edition Trinity is really one of the best things that they could have done. That way nobody's forced automatically make an earlier game have to end in darkness and despair because of a later games starting point.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that while \u00c6on isn't the future of Aberrant, Aberrant is the past of \u00c6on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288746#post1288746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know officially that they're not going to change it. It's the FSA and the America is basically a pit of dispair. And nothing says we have to keep it that way and I loan versions of the game. So I say why don't we come up with ideas on how either the darkness of the war could lead to something good or the FSA we could be only temporary for something better.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on this is to say that the Anima era was the low point for the FSA, and that it has been on the mend ever since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:40:22-08:00","id":1288779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288729#post1288729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't buy the notion that social or religious conservatives would like or stand for these developments, let alone being the driving force behind them. Which is why my approach is to introduce specific personalities that have subverted the groups in question (e.g., my reference to Reverend Nehemiah Scudder) as well as prominent inclusion of the non-subverted parts of these groups in the resistance against the FSA. (It's also why I can't take seriously shows like the Handmaiden's Tale or Revolution; they strike me as dealing with caricatures of conservatives rather than anything resembling the real thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>While I am totally on the left, I agree with you on the total lack of nuance in the standard portrayals of conservatives and their ideas. I find many ideas of conservatives bad and destructive, but they aren't Nazis or Fascists (even though I have enjoyed using the term as a slam).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-26-2021, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:11:48-08:00","id":1289008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288638#post1288638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given the resources and size of the USA, we are likely to be a power unless prevented from healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already a a given? The apocalypse happened and it happened in America. The Breadbasket of America is a wasteland full of mutants and Death. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know that dismissing the American people as worthless filth has become a trope. But the kind of crisis outlined has tended to bring positive growth in America's past, why assume a one-note corporate fascist state is the only future for America? Moreover, given that this world is heavily weighted toward China, why are we assuming that China, which is still proudly imperialist and ethnocentric doesn't demand the kind of power/control the USA is routinely accused of having now?[/quote]<br /> <br /> I presume a facist state is a profoundly optmistic take given the Aberrant War. Given that I would seriously consider just having America Gone. Like Americans are a refugee ethnicity in various parts of the world <br /> <br /> America has NEVER had a World war equivalent ravage it. That was America's big advantage in both world wars... no one fought in it. The idea that having worse than the devestation of two world wars happening in AMerica.. PLus not having a helpful AMerica there to help rebuild.. seems a situation where a functional and reasonably powerful country coming out is a BEST OF.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like it is taken as fact that the USA is the sole source of the world's evil and corruption. This is both silly and borders on several kinds of bigotry that deny adult agency to most human beings. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is the situation at all? Now there is definately some commentary on modern America, but given.. there was an appocalypse and America took the brunt of it. And if we look back at the Historical rise of Facism and Nazism it was driven by there destruction rained down by the first world war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the question, why not simply have a poorly recovered USA with competing visions of the good and the future. Corporations could, as in most of today's world, simply have too much power and thus imperial democracy. But there could be strong political movements fighting back. A divided decentralized USA prevents the people of the USA from having the power to fully reassert their rights. Corporations allied with religious and cultural conservatives could be fighting to maintain the fragmentation because it leaves them in the driver's seat. Outside groups like the Chinese, Norsa, or Proteus, all of whom dislike the idea of a revived America could aid the Corporate elites. This could give you a weakened America with cyberpunk stylings but it wouldn't be a bog standard &quot;EVIL AMERIKKKA!!&quot; In fact, the politics would be far livelier and there would be more chances for adventure and drama because the society would be in flux. Small scale victories could be achieved that changed lives for the better without being immediately followed by a Civil War. </div> </div> </div>So an america where other countries are playing Imperalistic proxy? I'm sure a Republic of Gilead is totally not a cliche. I&quot;m sure a New Confederacy would TOTALLY Not be a cliche and something that is original and never been done before.. &quot;America breaks up into a bunch of smaller countries&quot; is perhaps the most Cyberpunk cliche out there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:40:18-08:00","id":1289101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288638#post1288638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given the resources and size of the USA, we are likely to be a power unless prevented from healing. I know that dismissing the American people as worthless filth has become a trope. But the kind of crisis outlined has tended to bring positive growth in America's past, why assume a one-note corporate fascist state is the only future for America? Moreover, given that this world is heavily weighted toward China, why are we assuming that China, which is still proudly imperialist and ethnocentric doesn't demand the kind of power/control the USA is routinely accused of having now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The US won't have the same resources, due to having been one of the primary targets of the Aberrants during the war (the next being Europe, which is similarly devastated). And who says that China doesn't 'demand the kind of power/control' the USA wants now? That's one of the things that makes them as a superpower in a post-American world interesting. As agents of Aeon, you might have missions to observe, oppose or even support the spread of Chinese influence into another country or region.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288638#post1288638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like it is taken as fact that the USA is the sole source of the world's evil and corruption. This is both silly and borders on several kinds of bigotry that deny adult agency to most human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? It's a setting in a roleplaying game, and one that doesn't take it as fact that the USA is the sole source of the world's evil and corruption. It just explores the possibility that it could be one of them. 'America becomes a fascist state' isn't a statement of inevitability, it's an exploration of a frightening concept, the possibility that 'it could happen here!'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288638#post1288638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the question, why not simply have a poorly recovered USA with competing visions of the good and the future. Corporations could, as in most of today's world, simply have too much power and thus imperial democracy. But there could be strong political movements fighting back. A divided decentralized USA prevents the people of the USA from having the power to fully reassert their rights. Corporations allied with religious and cultural conservatives could be fighting to maintain the fragmentation because it leaves them in the driver's seat. Outside groups like the Chinese, Norsa, or Proteus, all of whom dislike the idea of a revived America could aid the Corporate elites. This could give you a weakened America with cyberpunk stylings but it wouldn't be a bog standard &quot;EVIL AMERIKKKA!!&quot; In fact, the politics would be far livelier and there would be more chances for adventure and drama because the society would be in flux. Small scale victories could be achieved that changed lives for the better without being immediately followed by a Civil War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because that's less interesting than 'USA as fascist-corporate state.' It's basically just 'America, like today, except poorer.' As for 'there would be more chances for adventure and drama,' I don't see it. There's plenty of adventure and drama to be had in authoritarian-USA: spying on the regime, dealing with resistance cells, smuggling refugees out of the country, counterespionage etc etc.<br /> <br /> Fascist USA isn't to your taste. But that's all it is - a matter of taste. The alternatives you're presenting aren't better, and IMO are far less interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T06:04:15-08:00","id":1289159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289101#post1289101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly because that's less interesting than 'USA as fascist-corporate state.' It's basically just 'America, like today, except poorer.' As for 'there would be more chances for adventure and drama,' I don't see it. There's plenty of adventure and drama to be had in authoritarian-USA: spying on the regime, dealing with resistance cells, smuggling refugees out of the country, counterespionage etc etc.<br /> <br /> Fascist USA isn't to your taste. But that's all it is - a matter of taste. The alternatives you're presenting aren't better, and IMO are far less interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if &quot;One note Fascist-Corporate state&quot; isn't an unimaginative fallback, why is Britain the same kind of mess? Remember North America is Cyberpunk, Europe is post-apocalyptic, and Australia is military sci fi, and everywhere else something more hopeful, so why repeat without variation, the same misery for Britain as for the USA? Come on our histories have diverged. With a post-apocalyptic waste in France and democratic nations nearby, it seems weird that Britain would be exactly the same kind of dictatorship.<br /> <br /> I think both the FSA and this setting's Britain are about a narrow political view rather than any kind of creativity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T08:51:03-08:00","id":1289197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289159#post1289159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if &amp;quot;One note Fascist-Corporate state&amp;quot; isn't an unimaginative fallback, why is Britain the same kind of mess? Remember North America is Cyberpunk, Europe is post-apocalyptic, and Australia is military sci fi, and everywhere else something more hopeful, so why repeat without variation, the same misery for Britain as for the USA? Come on our histories have diverged. With a post-apocalyptic waste in France and democratic nations nearby, it seems weird that Britain would be exactly the same kind of dictatorship.<br /> <br /> I think both the FSA and this setting's Britain are about a narrow political view rather than any kind of creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not the same, it\u2019s a different flavor of authoritarianism. The US is militaristic-fascist, the UK is Big Brother surveillance state. Each gives itself to different tropes.<br /> <br /> A better argument would be for Ukraine, which seems closer to the US, but even that\u2019s different enough to be worthwhile.<br /> <br /> As for \u2018a narrow political view,\u2019 I think the only politics on display here are your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:01:20-08:00","id":1289219,"title":"","content":"Oh really and what are his politics that are on display? *hard eyeroll*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:00:16-08:00","id":1289235,"title":"","content":"Indeed. If you had said that about me, that would have been one thing: I'm a solid conservative, and my objections to the way the FSA is handled are in part due to the clash between my understanding of conservatism and the supposed \u201cright-wing Fascist state\u201d that the FSA represents. <br /> <br /> But Astromancer is a self-declared leftist. If this was a matter of him projecting his politics into the setting, I'd expect him to be arguing <i>for</i> the FSA as presented, not calling it out as the result of a narrow political view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-18-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T13:09:45-08:00","id":1289278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289219#post1289219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh really and what are his politics that are on display? *hard eyeroll*</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1288043#post1288043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, America as Fascist wasteland is a worn out cliche. It has been decades since a positive and democratic vision of America's future has been part of popular culture. Rehashing this cliche seems right-wing as if the FSA and societies like it were less warnings and more wishes. America as hell hole has been done to death and each new iteration of the trope sounds more like praise of Fascism not a warning against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astromancer seems to be suggesting that OPP's presentation of a fascist US and UK is due to 'a narrow political view' rooted in fascism. Which strikes me as weird and counter-intuitive, but he's the one insisting that this is inherently terrible as opposed to simply not to his taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T13:19:49-08:00","id":1289288,"title":"","content":"I see the FSA as a Tragic Fall after the Abberant War. Understandable, but Tragic. I also don't see the FSA as anywhere as near as Monolothic as written. A lot of people are going to think &quot;Yeah, No. We saw what happened after PATRIOT ! &amp; II. No, thank you. We'll work with you on rebuilding and protecting against the Abberants. Beyond that, all bets are off.&quot; So, a lot of occasions of what has been termed 'Irish Democracy' will be present. and a lot of 'Undernet' activities. Go watch &quot;The Lives of Others&quot; if you want to lean the bleak route","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","user":"TheWanderingJewels","date":". 02-19-2019, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:30:00-08:00","id":1289628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289278#post1289278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Astromancer seems to be suggesting that OPP's presentation of a fascist US and UK is due to 'a narrow political view' rooted in fascism. Which strikes me as weird and counter-intuitive, but he's the one insisting that this is inherently terrible as opposed to simply not to his taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Less overt fascism than a cliche so worn out it is nearly toxic and working in reverse. Take stories where the protagonist lands in a society with reversed gender roles. The cliche is supposed to make people think about how unfair and arbitrary our society's gender roles are. The normal effect is to stigmatize women with power as cruel and unjust. The supposedly feminist cliche is instead anti-feminist in practice. <br /> <br /> By always showing the same fascist &quot;AMERIKKKA&quot; over and over, you normalize fascism and make it less of a threat and more simply a thing to endure/ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T13:44:30-08:00","id":1289634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289235#post1289235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. If you had said that about me, that would have been one thing: I'm a solid conservative, and my objections to the way the FSA is handled are in part due to the clash between my understanding of conservatism and the supposed \u201cright-wing Fascist state\u201d that the FSA represents.<br /> <br /> But Astromancer is a self-declared leftist. If this was a matter of him projecting his politics into the setting, I'd expect him to be arguing <i>for</i> the FSA as presented, not calling it out as the result of a narrow political view.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In each case Dataweaver we see the FSA as a trite worn out cliche. I agree with you that the take on conservative thought is grotesquely warped, I think most forms of conservatism are dangerously flawed, but that's no reason to slander people. The FSA strikes me as a pile of !9th and 20th century European Anti-American tropes reharshed through the prisms of The Frankfurt School and Critical Theory. A Fashionable hell future directed as a sort of atheistic divine curse on the USA. It presumes Arthur de Gobineau's racist rants dismissing America as a moral sewer by biological destiny are true.So if the goal is anti-fascist, the tools are so racist and proto-fascist as to promote fascism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:46:45-08:00","id":1289656,"title":"","content":"I will bring up a question. Aeon needed one post-apocalyptic and one Mega-Coorp setting.<br /> <br /> If you put Africa, Australia or South America as Apokaliptic, there would be no reason to make a character from this places. Almost the same happen wen you talk about facist SA, Africa or Australia, you have a place that is basically immigrant or black people (not African America, they are just African), so fascism here would be against the locals, not against foreigners (it\u2019s like this now, so...)<br /> <br /> China is the Grovernment centered country, and Japan is prety much cyberpunk now, just add some urban samurai and you got the idea.<br /> <br /> If you prefer Europe as facist, what makes sense as Italy, Spain, Germany, Portugal, and most of the Eastern Europe were facist at some point of XX century. <br /> <br /> US would be a great apocalyptic setting, as it\u2019s larger, have proportionally less population and would be the main target of most Aberrant (we already discussed it before). What do you think about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:12:59-08:00","id":1289663,"title":"","content":"It is less of a cliche and as several powers in the game setting would prefer a permanently weak USA it is logical. It would be better than the FSA. Plus, there would be more opportunities for setting lively RPG campaigns in the switch.<br /> <br /> It does bring up a major flaw in the setting. Many of the PCs strongly reflect Western values, I note the Pansexual Transexual Pop Singer in one supplement. How, in a world where the West is brutally eclipsed and illiberal nations proudly in the ascendant, do Western values of individual freedom and independent individuality survive and thrive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-19-2019, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:43:23-08:00","id":1289678,"title":"","content":"Africa and Sudamerica (at least on 2e) are quite liberals on all that matter individuality. They have even sex change, and it is reversible, they change skin colours freely and even have winks, horns and things like this, so I guess it\u2019s quite liberal on all aspects.<br /> I am quite sure in 1e was prety much the same in his aspect, Sudamerica is prety liberal and even the laws are \u201cliberal\u201d thanks to the Nor\u00e7a connections to Narcos. Africa was one setting I was not used, all I know it was united and respected all the African nations, so I guess they would respect any thing, as Africa is quite full of different cultures and traditions that would sound weird to our western culture.<br /> <br /> About the western view, I would say, after T2M and project utopia \u201cwesternised\u201d Africa and Middle East, it became more popular on the region, keeping this point of view later. Also, Australia became the new land of freedom and opportunities after the urban exodus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-19-2019, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:45:05-08:00","id":1289681,"title":"","content":"The only way I see it working is if, say, Africa becomes the new home for individual freedom and independent individuality. How that would happen, I'm not sure; but it would make the African Union make a bit more sense than it does right now: the various African cultures have historically been at each other's throats; and in order to have a Bright Continent, you need something to encourage disparate cultures to get along. If, somehow, the Western values of tolerance of those who are different from you somehow managed to make their way across the African continent, I could then see a cooperative transnational entity uniting the continent while respecting the separate cultures' distinctions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-10-2020, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:25:57-08:00","id":1289694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289678#post1289678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Africa and Sudamerica (at least on 2e) are quite liberals on all that matter individuality. They have even sex change, and it is reversible, they change skin colours freely and even have winks, horns and things like this, so I guess it\u2019s quite liberal on all aspects.<br /> I am quite sure in 1e was prety much the same in his aspect, Sudamerica is prety liberal and even the laws are \u201cliberal\u201d thanks to the Nor\u00e7a connections to Narcos. Africa was one setting I was not used, all I know it was united and respected all the African nations, so I guess they would respect any thing, as Africa is quite full of different cultures and traditions that would sound weird to our western culture.<br /> <br /> About the western view, I would say, after T2M and project utopia \u201cwesternised\u201d Africa and Middle East, it became more popular on the region, keeping this point of view later. Also, Australia became the new land of freedom and opportunities after the urban exodus.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Sudamerica, I'll note only that you can have a tremendous acceptance of biological diversity and still have zero tolerance for cultural and/or ideological differences. Africa, OTOH, is presented exactly as a culturally tolerant society; though as I said before, how they got that way is not immediately obvious.<br /> <br /> Actually, Australia, Oceania, and Luna are other possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-19-2019, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:58:10-08:00","id":1289703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289694#post1289694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On Sudamerica, I'll note only that you can have a tremendous acceptance of biological diversity and still have zero tolerance for cultural and/or ideological differences. Africa, OTOH, is presented exactly as a culturally tolerant society; though as I said before, how they got that way is not immediately obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say you are right about both. Sudamerica looks like the opposite of FSA, it\u2019s so \u201cLiberal\u201d that it turns around and start causing pressures to the population, if you are a little of the extreme you have a big problem.<br /> <br /> Africa, I have commented a few days ago, is one of my mais concerns about how it\u2019s possible. The differences between African nations are much bigger than the European, and we have Brexit. UAN would need to go thru something huge to exist. At same time, urban schism and the portable generator and makers make it possible to live your life in a remote place with no problems related to lack of technology or comunication, that can make it works. As I see, once you can keep your ville (not sure if it\u2019s the right word in the situation) with all that the population need, the fights against near villes are reduced a lot (it would not disappear, but reduce gradually) making it possible to interact on a civilised way more often.<br /> Still, it a HUGE step to unite all the continent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-19-2019, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:54:12-08:00","id":1289784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289703#post1289703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say you are right about both. Sudamerica looks like the opposite of FSA, it\u2019s so \u201cLiberal\u201d that it turns around and start causing pressures to the population, if you are a little of the extreme you have a big problem.<br /> <br /> Africa, I have commented a few days ago, is one of my mais concerns about how it\u2019s possible. The differences between African nations are much bigger than the European, and we have Brexit. UAN would need to go thru something huge to exist. At same time, urban schism and the portable generator and makers make it possible to live your life in a remote place with no problems related to lack of technology or comunication, that can make it works. As I see, once you can keep your ville (not sure if it\u2019s the right word in the situation) with all that the population need, the fights against near villes are reduced a lot (it would not disappear, but reduce gradually) making it possible to interact on a civilised way more often.<br /> Still, it a HUGE step to unite all the continent.</div> </div> </div> </div>A nasty plague that forced them to work together or die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:10:18-08:00","id":1289793,"title":"","content":"Across an entire continent?<br /> <br /> I do think there's something to be said about technological influences, in particular exemplify that don't require much infrastructure and OpNet access. But still, it's a tall order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T15:23:06-08:00","id":1290554,"title":"","content":"I just had a random idea of a variabt setting which could provide some basis for why and how America has become the FSA. <br /> <br /> America, with all of its Nova's took to the idea of the arcology tower. Within these multi mile tall Towers a single spiraling road went from bottom to top, with lots arranged around said road and the center shaft. Said Towers were a mix of residential, commercial, and industrial in rural, suburban, and urban landscapes. They were home to millions of people each. Even more they became very common, allowing for much of the rest of America to become a lot more nature. <br /> <br /> After the outbreak of hostilities something happened that would shock the rest of the world. A nova of some renown announced that if the people of Earth couldn't live with his people in peace and they would have to leave. Then, as one, all the arcology towers he owned or operated, which were most, activated some hidden engines and basically took off. They launched themselves into space before disappearing to some hyperspatial warp drive system.<br /> <br /> With them gone America lost much of its more intellectual and corporate elite. Which resulted in the movement that we later see, of the military and certain industrial complex forces working together to try to bridge the gap that occured. <br /> <br /> And yes if this seems familiar I'm pretty sure I already had the idea, but the difference is puttmg it as a reason fkr tge FSA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:08:23-08:00","id":1290601,"title":"","content":"Eh. It doesn't actually address any of the issues I have with the FSA; it just swaps out one catastrophe (the Blight) with another (the missing arcologies) while leaving the underlying assumptions intact (namely, that the military, corporations, and Christianity are \u201cone bad day\u201d away from establishing a fascist state).<br /> <br /> I actually kind of like the notion of swapping North America and Europe's respective futures, with North America getting decimated by the Aberrant War and largely ceasing to exist as a world power because what's left of the population is too occupied with plagues and mutant outbreaks to do anything meaningful in the international stage, or even to run a national government. Meanwhile, <i>Europe</i> is where a military police state has arisen. In this setup, I'd also reverse the \u201cprimary focus\u201d of the \u00c6sculapian Order and Orgotek, with the former focusing mainly in North America and the latter being headquartered in Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-21-2019, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:50:14-08:00","id":1290611,"title":"","content":"I would put the rex HQ somewhere in Mexico, in the border of the destruction, maybe there is even a wall. The big cities are corrupted ruins, part of the people that survived in the cities are sub Aberrants, and the last few places to live are the small cities and rural zones, but there is risk of invasion by sub aberrant zombies or quantum fallout, but many people still try to survive there to build up America again, or because the other countries are afraid of them to be sub Aberrants too.<br /> <br /> Facist Europe would be a extension of EU, with the crisis they start to force militarisation and border control to avoid Aberrants on the continent, expelling most of the immigrants and becoming highly facist. EU parlament suddenly became controlled by the militar and the companies related, until there is not much left of democracy there. The countries are still autonomous, but as much of the money flows thru EU and not the countries, they became dependent on the union, what keeps some diversity in the setting without breaking the facist condition. I would put France as a more democratic country, and Orgotech HQ is Paris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T18:51:38-08:00","id":1290625,"title":"","content":"Being fake upset at my idea's dismissal aside, (hehe), having Europe being a police state and America apocalyptic sounds great. Sounds perfect actually, especially when one considers how many and how powerful the novas there were in the Nova Age. It also makes sense as ground zero for the Aberrant War was in America. <br /> <br /> The fact that numerous quantum disturbances still exist could explain why its not healed or fixed, despite time and tech advancenent and the presence of psions. <br /> <br /> I also imagine some cities still exist within the former US that is still bastions of safety, high technology, and modern society. Maybe center such points of light on Chicago and the offices of Aeon Trinity, which survived and took over after the Collapse. <br /> <br /> Honestly. Thinking of this idea I have to say I really like it. <br /> <br /> I especially like it be because it allows for the adventure seed of sending psions and troops to still devasted America in order to fight quantum changed mutants and monsters. <br /> <br /> It also allows for stories of the need to send someone to an old American base or city to get that one thing that is needed to save the world. <br /> <br /> It also helps to explain Aeon's work tiwards unity, its located in a city surrounded by devastation and quantum aberrations. <br /> <br /> Yeah. I like making America in this setting apocalyptic and Europe a military police state - one recently tighted even more when the station fell down. I think that sounds perfect. <br /> <br /> I woukd totally use it if it had a focused outline and description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 02-21-2019, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T00:11:14-08:00","id":1290671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1290554#post1290554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a random idea of a variabt setting which could provide some basis for why and how America has become the FSA. <br /> <br /> America, with all of its Nova's took to the idea of the arcology tower. Within these multi mile tall Towers a single spiraling road went from bottom to top, with lots arranged around said road and the center shaft. Said Towers were a mix of residential, commercial, and industrial in rural, suburban, and urban landscapes. They were home to millions of people each. Even more they became very common, allowing for much of the rest of America to become a lot more nature. <br /> <br /> After the outbreak of hostilities something happened that would shock the rest of the world. A nova of some renown announced that if the people of Earth couldn't live with his people in peace and they would have to leave. Then, as one, all the arcology towers he owned or operated, which were most, activated some hidden engines and basically took off. They launched themselves into space before disappearing to some hyperspatial warp drive system.<br /> <br /> With them gone America lost much of its more intellectual and corporate elite. Which resulted in the movement that we later see, of the military and certain industrial complex forces working together to try to bridge the gap that occured. <br /> <br /> And yes if this seems familiar I'm pretty sure I already had the idea, but the difference is puttmg it as a reason fkr tge FSA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grr misclicked and erased my post.<br /> <br /> I like the context of putting that old setting idea of yours as part of why America collapsed being a lot of the intellectual and technological elite left.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t read up on the setting enough yet but that is a big deal to ignore how the UAN formed, you don\u2019t just become the New North America Over Night!?<br /> <br /> And if South America is super heavy on Shapeshifting tech that is going to be nuts on their Psyche, even if they stabilize the mores and values internally they undoubtedly would have much different values then every other continent by far.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of just making most of North America be a mutant infested Wasteland, I can have some 2000AD Judge Dread style Mega Cities composed of clusters of Arcologies, a few tiny holdouts in the Wasteland ala Fallout (New Vegas Please) andi personally would like then to just have a true heir or Successor of America be in either Luna, Mars, a Collection of O\u2019Neil Cylinders in the Astroid Belt and or Hawaii.<br /> <br /> And doesn\u2019t it feel a bit Off to just say oh yeah these impoverished countries are now the super powers of the World but only because of pure Luck/Plot device, and the previous Superpowers of the World, besides China, were essentially taken off the PlayingField because of Badluck/Plot Device. Isn\u2019t it a bit Pandery? And unintentionally awkward that once Europe finally because truly multicultural they also collapse into post Apocalyptic Wastelands and police states?<br /> <br /> I mean removing North America from the World stage means you remove over half the Worlds Medical Research, as well as a number of Technologies like Computer and military tech, and Hollywood is undesirable once the FSA become a thing, and the greatest Universities in the World are just no longer an option. This should have drastic changes across the World.<br /> <br /> Since I\u2019m not familiar yet with the setting how is Israel, Egypt, and the countries of the Former Soviet Union, and China doing by the time of Aeon? Did China ever take out the Dalai Lama?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:58:29-08:00","id":1290696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1290671#post1290671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of just making most of North America be a mutant infested Wasteland, I can have some 2000AD Judge Dread style Mega Cities composed of clusters of Arcologies, a few tiny holdouts in the Wasteland ala Fallout (New Vegas Please) andi personally would like then to just have a true heir or Successor of America be in either Luna, Mars, a Collection of O\u2019Neil Cylinders in the Astroid Belt and or Hawaii.<br /> <br /> And doesn\u2019t it feel a bit Off to just say oh yeah these impoverished countries are now the super powers of the World but only because of pure Luck/Plot device, and the previous Superpowers of the World, besides China, were essentially taken off the PlayingField because of Badluck/Plot Device. Isn\u2019t it a bit Pandery? And unintentionally awkward that once Europe finally because truly multicultural they also collapse into post Apocalyptic Wastelands and police states?<br /> <br /> I mean removing North America from the World stage means you remove over half the Worlds Medical Research, as well as a number of Technologies like Computer and military tech, and Hollywood is undesirable once the FSA become a thing, and the greatest Universities in the World are just no longer an option. This should have drastic changes across the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more like a zombie apokalypse, but Fallout and Dread is an nice option. Big bad monsters wandering the ruins and fields... it makes a lot more sense. You can even have a kind of Subaberrant rising society, with the regentes grouping up to make their life\u2019s less horrible...<br /> <br /> One thing I don\u2019t get on FSA is, a militaristic facist country with the largest military and thousands of nuclear transcontinental missiles, as soon as there is any kind of pressure from a smal country or even Sudamerica, they would point the guns and force people to react. It worked with North Korea and they don\u2019t have all that military budget. FSA would not fall easily and not without war... so Apokaliptic States of American would be more... how can I say... plausible...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:38:10-08:00","id":1290736,"title":"","content":"The whole Aeon setting is more like the aftershock of a Reality Quake with random game settings illogically stitched together. It is poorly thought out in so many ways. I noted that the six groups in the original Aeon Binder/Book were Corporate Elites (Electrokinetics), Soulless Bureaucracy (Telepaths), Organised Religion (Clairsentients), Big Military ( Telekinetics), Organised Crime (Biokinetics), and Corporate Medicine (Vitakinetics). When we meet them the Teleporters were survivalists. I suggested that as a means to bring on a new world of peace and justice (freedom and fairness are clearly excluded) these people don't inspire confidence.<br /> <br /> The fact that New Agey mystical Viakinetics had their own center in Haiti and the change of Norca from Narcoterrorists to Ecoterrorists doesn't really make the setting any more hopeful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-22-2019, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:57:23-08:00","id":1290899,"title":"","content":"Yeah Aeon is fun because it handles so many Genres, but also it stretches credulity because it tries to fit in so many Genres. You can\u2019t have Star Trek, and Mass Effect and Fallout, and Judge Dredd at the same time, it makes little sense. It can be fun though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T14:26:48-08:00","id":1290905,"title":"","content":"At least not on the same planet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:17:40-08:00","id":1290934,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s probably the reason Aberrant is so much more famous than Trinity. But I do like the systemic view of the setting and the meta plot... I really loved all that I played on 1e, much of space exploration and war, some conspiration... actually a lot conspiration by the end... and the plot twists...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T16:07:46-08:00","id":1366878,"title":"","content":"An easier way to deal with the setting is that the book as presented is as Planetary Authorities wish the place as presented. There is always degrees in any setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T17:03:32-08:00","id":1366883,"title":"","content":"Holy dark powers of necromancy Batman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T17:10:42-08:00","id":1366885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheWanderingJewels</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1366878#post1366878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An easier way to deal with the setting is that the book as presented is as Planetary Authorities wish the place as presented. There is always degrees in any setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh that's an interesting twist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:17:31-08:00","id":1367528,"title":"","content":"You know, America being torn into a number of competing (semi-hostile) countries following disaster of some kind if not just descending into a hellscape dotted with city states really seems to be the cliche. Outside of <b><i>Judge Dredd</i></b> -- which is basically every crap-sack future ever -- the fascist junta is comparatively rare as American futures in pop culture go; assuming lack of apocalypse as definitive event, usually it's the megacorp (cyberpunk) dystopia.<br /> <br /> Given the genre-splatification was an edict forced onto the setting from on high by White Wolf's bosses and not what the designers had originally intended, I had hoped that 2e while obviously beholden to its predecessor would have felt a bit more nuanced in presenting the non-western ascendency to a predominantly western audience but limited space is limited space I guess.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25951-1001100x02","name":"1001100x02","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:55:29-08:00","id":1367533,"title":"","content":"Honestly, for me, the events going onon Earth in Aeon are literally something I care zero about. Mostly because I am not really a fan of the way the world is presented. <br /> <br /> (Truthfully its the same with Aberrant, I'm not a fan of how the natioms of the world are set up.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:22:04-08:00","id":1367606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1001100x02</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1367528#post1367528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, America being torn into a number of competing (semi-hostile) countries following disaster of some kind if not just descending into a hellscape dotted with city states really seems to be the cliche. Outside of <b><i>Judge Dredd</i></b> -- which is basically every crap-sack future ever -- the fascist junta is comparatively rare as American futures in pop culture go; assuming lack of apocalypse as definitive event, usually it's the megacorp (cyberpunk) dystopia.</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, my issue with the FSA isn't whether or not it's cliche; it's whether or not it's believable. And even the \u201cmilitary junta allowed with megacorps\u201d isn't something I find unbelievable; only the choice of culprits. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1001100x02</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1367528#post1367528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the genre-splatification was an edict forced onto the setting from on high by White Wolf's bosses and not what the designers had originally intended, I had hoped that 2e while obviously beholden to its predecessor would have felt a bit more nuanced in presenting the non-western ascendency to a predominantly western audience but limited space is limited space I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware of the genre-splatification being an edict forced into the setting from on high. That said, it's pretty much a moot point: the \u201cpowers on high\u201d are gone, but so are the original developers. <br /> <br /> Still, I'm curious how you would have done it differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:19:27-08:00","id":1367830,"title":"","content":"Trinity world was always an RPG setting first. It does lack lived in history so to say. That is not really the issue, because the game lines were always metaplot driven first(Insert Abberant second edition rant here). It is just not smart to delve deep into the backgrounds as the setting really does not hold up water to a significant degree and honestly never quite did.<br /> It does have bland corporatist junta, si you can have your cyberpunk adventure, that is all there is to it. Is it kinda bland and nonsensical in the large scheme, yes, but it does not quite matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:03:15-08:00","id":1367859,"title":"","content":"Had to double check to see if it was this thread or the other eerily similar thread where I made this statement, but I feel like the FSA section in 2e makes a lot more sense if you flip back and forth to the timeline to remember that all of the formative events of the FSA happen during the Aberrant War. On top of that, if you keep in mind that the USA was arguably the front line of the whole conflict, getting the brunt of the carnage, the situation seems just dire enough for things to go the way they do.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it ain't perfect, it tries to drive the point home a little too far sometimes, but it isn't so easily dismissed either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:12:33-08:00","id":1367887,"title":"","content":"Any setting made by a limited number of people will lack something from the point of view of others. In the end Aeon time line has a better foundation than most of the modern and post-apocalipse settings.<br /> <br /> I would change only a few things (immigration to FSA for sure, replacing the immigrants by regular poor people and the regular people by robots create a similar effect). But I really don\u2019t plan to go deep into any of this aspects in my games... I do prefere the space stuff (Portal core screaming: Space Space Space!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T15:23:23-08:00","id":1368416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1367887#post1367887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any setting made by a limited number of people will lack something from the point of view of others. In the end Aeon time line has a better foundation than most of the modern and post-apocalipse settings.<br /> <br /> I would change only a few things (immigration to FSA for sure, replacing the immigrants by regular poor people and the regular people by robots create a similar effect). But I really don\u2019t plan to go deep into any of this aspects in my games... I do prefere the space stuff (Portal core screaming: Space Space Space!)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting tidbit here and I think it bears thinking about. First edition was heavily metaplot driven and in retrospect, trinity is unmoored without it. Aeon does get off lightly, because the metaplot is still there,unlike Aberrant(insert second Aberrant second edition rant here), but it feels like the focus on metaplot did more good in case of trinity unlike WoD and its loss at least to me seems to be a significant loss to the setting in retrospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:04:12-07:00","id":1374065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1286187#post1286187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the 1st ed. they were a mafia-like group with political pretentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, they are nothing like that in 2nd ed. We tweaked all the Psi Orders a bit, but they are the Legions were two we looked at and gave a great big nope - mercenaries are not heroic (as I stated in my setting bible, written many years ago now, when I think of mercs, I think Blackwater &amp; Erik Prince), and having the South American psi order be a narco-gang was from my PoV deeply offensive. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:45:29-07:00","id":1374071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheWanderingJewels</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1287783#post1287783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lean Libertarian &amp; Classical liberal myself, but I can see how the FSA ended up the way it did. The USA lead the pack on integration of Nova\u2019s into society which went rather badly as the instability of the Nova\u2019s turned Abberants started to become apparent. Given the standard heavy handedness that Homeland Security (and law enforcement in general) tends to pull to respond to problems caused the situation to escalate quickly.<br /> <br /> Now combine this with the standard news feed which is more interested in creating controversy and conflict to make money and preserve the status quo (in spite of pretensions otherwise). Most of the regular media does this. Now add some really pissed off Abberants who\u2019d prefer to be left to their own devices and have rapidly grown in power. Give even just a basic few of them tactics and the ability to go after the people actually making the decisions to make there lives miserable and things will spiral fast.<br /> <br /> Level a major city or two by both sides and shit gets real real fast, real no sense of humor locking things down and trying to wipe the Aberrants out. This turns out about as well as one would think. I also imagine the Abberants going after anyone making Anti-Abberant propaganda. As political ideology likely won\u2019t mean much too them, they will hit news, entertainment, and government outlets equally to get the message makers too frightened to speak out.<br /> Now add the other events we see. Wycoff in particular as that cripples food production, and when it comes to survival and prevention of food riots, the rules go out the window, and the surviving government declares martial law and rolls out the military to grab food production centers (and worrying about Abberants become a much less priority) and try to keep things stable.<br /> <br /> Local stabilization is likely to be rough for a while as the various Area commands try to stabilize things so that people can eat properly. Vertical farming will be rather expensive, but needed, so that would eat into budgets needing to go elsewhere, so you would get some of that lovely dystopia vibe.<br /> <br /> You also will get calls for Unity as that will be needed to get things back up and running in a sane manner. That will likely mean suppression of anything outside of the party line and rebuilding the population (The start of Totalitarianism). Anything else will be frowned on, but unless it\u2019s an immediate threat, local commands will have better things to do. That said, anything that is perceived to threaten social stability and order is likely to get it in the back of the head with a coilgun. So Modernism &amp; Post-modernism and it\u2019s derivations get chucked out the window hard.<br /> <br /> That means the Entertainment &amp; News sector is going to get a visit from Homeland with explicit instructions on what they will do to help rebuild society. The few that resist won\u2019t exist anymore, and the rest will get the message, if not comply willingly when first asked. Education at all levels will be reconfigured to what is needed to help rebuild. It\u2019s not nice, but it is logical.<br /> <br /> Now give it about 60 years, and you get the FSA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said. It's also important to keep in mind how much of a mess the US was well before Wycoff detonated. 7 years before that half of Florida was destroyed, killing a not insignificant portion of the US population in an instant. Then there are all the battles between novas/Aberrants and between humans and Aberrants in between 2054 to 2061. The US had a significantly higher proportion of the world population of novas than any other nation, and when they started going ultra-violent most of then did so in the US. So, the US was already in deeply terrible shape with a panicked population, and an economy that was a serious mess, and then Wycoff killed off most of US agriculture. You didn't have a robust and thriving nation suddenly facing food shortages, you have a nation that looked only slightly better than France or Germany in 1946, and then its facing food shortages. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:57:40-07:00","id":1374072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1289703#post1289703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say you are right about both. Sudamerica looks like the opposite of FSA, it\u2019s so \u201cLiberal\u201d that it turns around and start causing pressures to the population, if you are a little of the extreme you have a big problem.<br /> <br /> Africa, I have commented a few days ago, is one of my mais concerns about how it\u2019s possible. The differences between African nations are much bigger than the European, and we have Brexit. UAN would need to go thru something huge to exist. At same time, urban schism and the portable generator and makers make it possible to live your life in a remote place with no problems related to lack of technology or comunication, that can make it works. As I see, once you can keep your ville (not sure if it\u2019s the right word in the situation) with all that the population need, the fights against near villes are reduced a lot (it would not disappear, but reduce gradually) making it possible to interact on a civilised way more often.<br /> Still, it a HUGE step to unite all the continent.</div> </div> </div> </div>My initial vision of Sudamerica and the UAN (which was then changed and built upon in many awesome ways by several excellent authors) was that Sudamerica is a mostly positive vision of the future of the US - there's some inequality and corruption, but things are mostly headed in the right direction, and while the Gini Quotient isn't ideal, it's still a region where freedom is both real and important and where abject poverty is gone, and people can meaningfully hope for a better life. Meanwhile, the UAN is the a similar vision of the EU - a vast multicultural social democracy with vast differences, but also a common sense of purpose, and a serious commitment to care for all of its citizens. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T04:14:37-07:00","id":1374097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1374065#post1374065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, they are nothing like that in 2nd ed. We tweaked all the Psi Orders a bit, but they are the Legions were two we looked at and gave a great big nope - mercenaries are not heroic (as I stated in my setting bible, written many years ago now, when I think of mercs, I think Blackwater &amp; Erik Prince), and having the South American psi order be a narco-gang was from my PoV deeply offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>So just to clarify the big orders are supposed to be heroic, even if they their reputations are slandered like the Quanta Ks. Its offensive to not make Orders idealized and heroic because they are based off of Region/Culture but individual nations are allowed to be the opposite of this like Mexico being a Totalitarian Dystopia of inequality? I'm confused why that is fine but South America had to tone down drugs, crimelords, and violence.<br /> <br /> Its not a concern that the perception of a double standard can be deeply offensive?<br /> <br /> And again I think the Cataclysm of Florida being destroyed and major Wastelands from Nova conflicts are a strong point in forming the FSA. Its a lot more viable that crazy stuff happens because honestly most any large nation could do a 180 after a disaster of that magnitude as things are no longer predicatable and any number of factions could rise to power in the chaos. Its that framework I feel that can build towards making a more viable backstory for something like the FSA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T19:04:03-07:00","id":1374853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1374097#post1374097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So just to clarify the big orders are supposed to be heroic, even if they their reputations are slandered like the Quanta Ks. Its offensive to not make Orders idealized and heroic because they are based off of Region/Culture but individual nations are allowed to be the opposite of this like Mexico being a Totalitarian Dystopia of inequality? I'm confused why that is fine but South America had to tone down drugs, crimelords, and violence.<br /> <br /> Its not a concern that the perception of a double standard can be deeply offensive?<br /> <br /> And again I think the Cataclysm of Florida being destroyed and major Wastelands from Nova conflicts are a strong point in forming the FSA. Its a lot more viable that crazy stuff happens because honestly most any large nation could do a 180 after a disaster of that magnitude as things are no longer predicatable and any number of factions could rise to power in the chaos. Its that framework I feel that can build towards making a more viable backstory for something like the FSA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its offensive to make the Orders of such dubious and questionable morality that they seem borderline villainous, because they are almost universally going to be one of your Paths if you're playing a Psion of their associated aptitude.<br /> Choosing to have your character be associated with a morally dubious drug cartel is all fine and dandy, but when that association is all but forced upon you simply because you want to play a biokinetic then that can kinda suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25279-elowin","user":"Elowin","date":". 03-14-2020, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25279-elowin","name":"Elowin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T22:09:09-07:00","id":1374876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elowin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1285885-necro-why-such-a-boring-future-usa?p=1374853#post1374853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its offensive to make the Orders of such dubious and questionable morality that they seem borderline villainous, because they are almost universally going to be one of your Paths if you're playing a Psion of their associated aptitude.<br /> Choosing to have your character be associated with a morally dubious drug cartel is all fine and dandy, but when that association is all but forced upon you simply because you want to play a biokinetic then that can kinda suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep - that's about 60% of the issue - there was *way* too much emphasis on the Orders and the Aeon Trinity being morally pretty dark grey in 1e. This setting is about heroes and heroism, and while it's awesome storytelling to have there be bad actors in various Orders or in the Aeon Trinity, the whole point of the setting is that most people aren't evil or actively abetting evil and corruption. As a result, when the PCs find the villains within the Order or the Aeon Trinity, and pass their evidence to the organization's leaders, the people and the problems they created will actually be dealt with, not swept under the rug. <br /> <br /> The other 40% of the reason is that each Order is tied to a location and is in some sense the exemplar of that nation or region - and having the exemplar for South America be a drug cartel is not a good look. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}